never have time to try.\n\nRepo:","url":"https://x.com/ShopifyEng/status/2044477537200550383","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/since-we-open-sourced-pi-autoresearch-shopify-teams-have-been-running-it-on-everything-results-s-twi5gkhmr","summary":null,"image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--ZrL_HSsR--/f_auto/v1722860399/public/Placeholder%2006","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-04-16T05:28:17.647Z"},{"id":"tOAwZ4yBi","title":"Shipping support for module script integrity in Chrome & Safari","url":"https://shopify.engineering/shipping-support-for-module-script-integrity-in-chrome-safari","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/shipping-support-for-module-script-integrity-in-chrome-safari-toawz4ybi","summary":"Shopify has implemented Subresource Integrity (SRI) for imported JavaScript modules in Chrome and Safari, enhancing security by ensuring module scripts haven't been tampered with. This initiative involved integrating integrity metadata into import maps, allowing dynamic imports with verified integrity. The feature has successfully shipped in Chrome 127 and is in Safari 18 Beta, making ES modules and dynamic imports safer to use with SRI.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/802e5190cf71073099361c0d1de4c4f6?_a=AQAEuiZ","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-08-02T17:17:47.000Z"},{"id":"2jpUnIQt6","title":"Improving Shopify App\u2019s Performance","url":"https://shopify.engineering/improving-shopify-app-s-performance","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/improving-shopify-app-s-performance-2jpuniqt6","summary":"Shopify shares their journey of improving their app's performance, achieving a significant increase in app launch speed and reduced screen load times.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/dfa6a3ba7a69e6c5ebe227c85b8adbdd?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":4,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-03-05T20:37:37.000Z"},{"id":"bdqbqhLZC","title":"A Packwerk Retrospective","url":"https://shopify.engineering/a-packwerk-retrospective","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/a-packwerk-retrospective-bdqbqhlzc","summary":"Packwerk is a tool developed by Shopify to enforce boundaries and modularize Rails applications. It helps decouple code and organize it into well-defined packages. However, it has weaknesses and blind spots, such as difficulty in defining packages correctly and resolving violations, and limited tracking of dynamically generated constants. Shopify is rethinking how they organize their monolith, focusing on running code and functional units rather than domains.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/9a9a42950f17439ec973c4e394102e45?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-02-07T21:40:35.000Z"},{"id":"LcnezmROa","title":"Horizontally scaling the Rails backend of Shop app with Vitess","url":"https://shopify.engineering/horizontally-scaling-the-rails-backend-of-shop-app-with-vitess","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/horizontally-scaling-the-rails-backend-of-shop-app-with-vitess-lcnezmroa","summary":"The post discusses the process of horizontally scaling the Rails backend of the Shop app using Vitess. It covers the challenges faced, the benefits of using Vitess, and the steps involved in the migration.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/77a1abcc767580cf5c2286ca6763ab5c?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-01-17T20:34:53.000Z"},{"id":"j5lQcyFCu","title":"Getting Started with React Native Skia","url":"https://shopify.engineering/getting-started-with-react-native-skia","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/getting-started-with-react-native-skia-j5lqcyfcu","summary":"Learn about the basics of React Native Skia, including its use-case, drawing in Skia, and adding movement to drawings using react-native-reanimated.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/11a04016d2b83ce9107e40256d913415?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":4,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-12-04T15:00:03.000Z"},{"id":"0lHvz8Dq5","title":"Introducing Ruvy","url":"https://shopify.engineering/introducing-ruvy","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/introducing-ruvy-0lhvz8dq5","summary":"Ruvy is a toolchain that takes Ruby code and creates a WebAssembly module. It provides performance improvements by pre-initializing the Ruby virtual machine and simplifying the execution of the Wasm module. Ruvy is different from ruby.wasm in how it handles file access and initialization. Benchmark results show that Ruvy modules have faster runtime and compilation times compared to ruby.wasm modules. Ruvy does not require specifying file paths as WASI arguments, making it compatible with different computing environments. The project is open sourced and contributions are welcome.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/741cf3edde85f331cab1ca732eabad6b?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":6,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-10-18T13:43:29.000Z"},{"id":"ixHbmX8wU","title":"Building a ShopifyQL Code Editor","url":"https://shopify.engineering/building-a-shopifyql-code-editor","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/building-a-shopifyql-code-editor-ixhbmx8wu","summary":"ShopifyQL is an accessible, commerce-focused querying language used on both the client and server. The language is defined by an ANTLR grammar and is used to generate code for multiple targets. CodeMirror, a code editor framework built for the web, has its own grammar & parser engine called Lezer.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/6e30f6ae30c93026cab2be2f1a6d2ebe?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-09-11T14:02:54.000Z"},{"id":"vnGnehGuJ","title":"Sidekick\u2019s Improved Streaming Experience","url":"https://shopify.engineering/sidekicks-improved-streaming-experience","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/sidekick-s-improved-streaming-experience-vngnehguj","summary":"Sidekick\u2019s Improved Streaming Experience (2023) In the realm of Large Language Model (LLM) chatbots, two of the most persistent user experience disruptions relate to streaming of responses. Markdown rendering jank: Syntax fragments being rendered as raw text until they form a complete Markdown element.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/e1ca0fdbf996fa06c70af18c8eae66c1?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-08-01T20:08:07.000Z"},{"id":"dH25g2Dpn","title":"Shopify\u2019s platform is the Web platform","url":"https://shopify.engineering/shopifys-platform-is-the-web-platform","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/shopify-s-platform-is-the-web-platform-dh25g2dpn","summary":"Shopify\u2019s platform is the Web platform (2023) Remix for Shopify Apps TL;DR Remix is now the recommended way to build Admin apps on Shopify. With Remix, you get a best-in-class developer experience while ensuring exceptional out-of-the-box performance for your app.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/89e660875ebca6c7548acb85289e3030?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":4,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-07-26T15:51:33.000Z"}],"similar_handles":["KRAZAM","benjojo","ntietz","serverlesslife","doordash"],"opposite_handles":["dailydevworld","on_leuwcq","horde","watercooler","dotnetsquad"],"similar":[{"id":"KRAZAM","handle":"KRAZAM","name":"KRAZAM","is_squad":false,"x":1.1672,"y":-0.84,"cluster_id":3,"posts_collected":39,"image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--1kRG_HZU--/f_auto/v1716024949/logos/KRAZAM","features_preview":{"posts_per_week":0.383812,"median_upvotes":0.0,"author_present_share":0.0,"hype_score":0.0,"avg_read_time":3.769231,"tag_diversity":0.897436},"top_tags_preview":[["cloudflare",2],["machine-learning",2],["ai",2]],"view_coords":{"engagement_style":[-5.2647,-1.2647],"